# bbb-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: on BBB you may not need any of them.
#
# `--mode search` and `--mode category` read BBB's own JSON endpoint, which
# is NOT behind Cloudflare. Measured 2026-09-16 from a datacenter VPS that
# gets HTTP 403 on every HTML page on the site: HTTP 200, 57 KB, 15 complete
# business records. A two-page run from that machine with this file absent
# returned 30 rows and `status: complete`. No key, no proxy, no account.
#
# What the credentials below buy is `--mode profile`, which is the one page
# kind BBB gates — and there is no endpoint for it, so the rendered page is
# the only route to accreditation dates, complaint counts and the rest.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU BUY SOLVING FOR THIS SITE. BBB refuses in two
# shapes and only one of them is solvable:
#
#   "Just a moment..." with a Turnstile widget   a real challenge. This is
#                                                what a solver is for.
#   "You have been blocked | Better Business     a refusal. No widget, no
#    Bureau(R)"                                  sitekey, nothing to solve —
#                                                a solve here buys nothing.
#
# Both answer HTTP 403 and both wear BBB's own branding in the title, which
# is why the scrapers tell them apart structurally rather than by the title.
# From a datacenter address the second is what arrives, and what clears it is
# the EXIT, not a solver. Solving is wired up and capped at one purchase per
# page; it is not the happy path here.
#
# This key IS what --fingerprint uses (a separate subscription from solving:
# a working solver key is not automatically enabled for fingerprints, and the
# client says so by name if it is not).
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint, and on this site it is what
# makes `--mode profile` work at all.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. Use `country-us` (or `country-ca`):
#             BBB is a US and Canadian directory, and a datacenter address is
#             refused wherever it is. Measured: a `country-us` profile was
#             served normally where a German datacenter VPS got 403 on every
#             request, byte-identical over six polls.
#   pid-      is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account — reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one. That is also why --concurrency is
#             refused with --cdp-endpoint: several workers would collide.
#
# Note that Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes
# a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer
# authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work. selenium_scraper.py refuses
# a credentialed endpoint with exit 2 and says which engine to use instead —
# so `--mode profile` is the one mode that needs a specific engine.
#
# One more thing to expect: a credential here does not last. Of the eight
# Scraping Browser profiles and six proxy logins inherited from this
# family's sibling repos, exactly one still authenticated when this repo was
# written; the rest returned 401 `deny_no_user` or 407. That is why the
# canary workflow is dispatch-only rather than nightly.
BBB_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A residential exit for `--mode profile`. One URL here, or --proxy-file with
# one per line for a pool; a pool is what spreads a run's volume, and
# --concurrency without one just sends N times the traffic from a single
# address.
#
# Region: BBB serves the US and Canada, so `-region-us` or `-region-ca`. What
# the site scores is the ADDRESS rather than its geography — but it scores a
# datacenter address in any country, so a residential one is not optional
# for the profile path.
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that
# engine strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
#
# Not needed for the two listing modes. See the note at the top.
BBB_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@na.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. BBB serves the United States and Canada from ONE
# host, `www.bbb.org`, with the country in the PATH — so there is no
# per-country hostname to get wrong, and `find_country=USA|CAN` (or the
# `--country` flag) is what selects the directory.
#
# The three URL kinds, one per mode:
#
#   /search?find_text=…&find_loc=…       --mode search. `?page=N` addresses
#                                        every page, up to the 15 BBB serves.
#   /{cc}/category/{slug}                --mode category. The slug is a human
#                                        address; the endpoint filters on a
#                                        numeric tobId, which the scraper
#                                        resolves from BBB's own response.
#   /{cc}/{st}/{city}/profile/{cat}/{n}  --mode profile. One page, and the
#                                        only one that is Cloudflare-gated.
#
# `--text` and `--location` build a search URL for you, so this is optional
# even for a search.
BBB_URL=https://www.bbb.org/search?find_country=USA&find_text=restaurants&find_loc=New+York%2C+NY

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
